Core's NOTICE records the design's origin: the report shell (the "V9" developer-console design:
styles, layout, navigation palette, section structure and the sample content shown in
demonstration mode) is extracted and adapted from the legacy ai-harness project, file
src/report/templates/local-report-v9.html at commit f5d5f84b9006b628778983dab56dd92dc8888156
(https://github.com/samartomar/ai-harness/tree/f5d5f84b9006b628778983dab56dd92dc8888156).
That project is Copyright 2026 The AI Harness (aih) authors and is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Changes from that file: product naming and legacy commands were removed
from the shell, the baked-in sample sections remain only as the labelled demonstration sample,
a hydration function and a few styles were added, and the radar and heatmap scripts were
guarded so they only run when their elements exist.

Changes in the Workbench: the renderer receives @aihq/core/report's public importSnapshot and
exportSnapshot from its caller (createReportRenderer) instead of importing Core's private data
module, and the template module is generated by tools/report-template.mjs. The rendered bytes
are unchanged.

The design uses system font stacks only. No font files, images or third-party scripts are
embedded or loaded.
